{"id":"mahabharata-7-106","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":106,"title":"षडधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 106 · Karna and Bhima, first duel","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks about the duel of Karna and Bhima near Arjuna's chariot. Karna wounds Bhima with ease and Bhima, smiling, challenges him, and in the end Bhima breaks his bow.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನ ರಥದ ಬಳಿ ಕರ್ಣ-ಭೀಮರ ದ್ವಂದ್ವದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಣ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಸುಲಭವಾಗಿ ಗಾಯಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ನಗುತ್ತಾ ಭೀಮ ಸವಾಲು ಹಾಕುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೊನೆಗೆ ಭೀಮ ಕರ್ಣನ ಬಿಲ್ಲನ್ನು ಮುರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र अर्जुन के रथ के पास कर्ण और भीम के द्वन्द्व के बारे में पूछते हैं। कर्ण सहजता से भीम को घायल करता है, भीम मुस्कुराकर चुनौती देते हैं, और अन्त में भीम कर्ण का धनुष तोड़ देते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుని రథం దగ్గర కర్ణ భీముల ద్వంద్వం గురించి ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. కర్ణుడు భీముని సులభంగా గాయపరుస్తాడు, భీముడు నవ్వుతూ సవాలు చేస్తాడు; చివరికి భీముడు కర్ణుని విల్లు విరుస్తాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனனின் தேரருகே கர்ணன் பீமனின் தனிப்போரைப் பற்றித் த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். கர்ணன் பீமனை எளிதில் காயப்படுத்த, பீமன் புன்னகையுடன் சவால் விடுத்து இறுதியில் கர்ணனின் வில்லை முறிக்கிறான்.","ml":"അർജുനന്റെ തേരിനടുത്തുള്ള കർണ്ണന്റെയും ഭീമന്റെയും ദ്വന്ദ്വയുദ്ധത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കർണ്ണൻ അനായാസം ഭീമനെ മുറിവേൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമൻ പുഞ്ചിരിയോടെ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വെല്ലുവിളിക്കുന്നു, ഒടുവിൽ കർണ്ണന്റെ വില്ല് ഭീമൻ തകർക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.106; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यौ तौ कर्णश्च भीमश्च संप्रयुद्धौ महाबलौ ।\nअर्जुनस्य रथोपान्ते कीदृशः सोऽभवद्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two strong men, Karna and Bhima, who fought together near Arjuna's chariot, what was that battle like?"}},{"n":2,"text":"पूर्वं हि निर्जितः कर्णो भीमसेनेन संयुगे ।\nकथं भूयस्तु राधेयो भीममागान्महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna was beaten earlier by Bhimasena in the fight; how did Radheya, the great chariot-warrior, come again against Bhima?"}},{"n":3,"text":"भीमो वा सूततनयं प्रत्युद्यातः कथं रणे ।\nमहारथसमाख्यातं पृथिव्यां प्रवरं रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or how did Bhima advance in battle against the charioteer's son, called the foremost chariot-warrior on earth?"}},{"n":4,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणावतिक्रम्य धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनान्यतो भयमादत्त विना कर्णं धनुर्धरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, past Bhishma and Drona, took fear from no one else except the archer Karna."}},{"n":5,"text":"भयान्न शेते सततं चिन्तयन्वै महारथम् ।\nतं कथं सूतपुत्रं हि भीमोऽयुध्यत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Constantly through fear he cannot sleep, thinking of that great chariot-warrior. How then did Bhima fight the charioteer's son in the battle?"}},{"n":6,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यं वीर्यसंपन्नं समरेष्वनिवर्तिनम् ।\nकथं कर्णं युधां श्रेष्ठं भीमोऽयुध्यत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did Bhima fight Karna, devoted to Brahmins, rich in valor, never turning back in battles, the best of fighters?"}},{"n":7,"text":"यौ तौ समीयतुर्वीरावर्जुनस्य रथं प्रति ।\nकथं नु तावयुध्येतां सूतपुत्रवृकोदरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did those two, the charioteer's son and Vrikodara, fight, who met near Arjuna's chariot?"}},{"n":8,"text":"भ्रातृत्वं दर्शितं पूर्वं घृणी चापि स सूतजः ।\nकथं भीमेन युयुधे कुन्त्या वाक्यमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brotherhood was shown to him before, and that charioteer's son is compassionate; how did he fight Bhima, remembering Kunti's words?"}},{"n":9,"text":"भीमो वा सूतपुत्रेण स्मरन्वैरं पुरा कृतम् ।\nसोऽयुध्यत कथं वीरः कर्णेन सह संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or how did the hero Bhima fight Karna in battle, remembering the old enmity done by the charioteer's son?"}},{"n":10,"text":"आशास्ते च सदा सूत पुत्रो दुर्योधनो मम ।\nकर्णो जेष्यति संग्रामे सहितान्पाण्डवानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always, Sanjaya, my son Duryodhana hopes that Karna will defeat all the Pandavas together in battle."}},{"n":11,"text":"जयाशा यत्र मन्दस्य पुत्रस्य मम संयुगे ।\nस कथं भीमकर्माणं भीमसेनमयुध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"My dull son, whose hope of victory lies in him, how did he fight Bhimasena of terrible deeds?"}},{"n":12,"text":"यं समाश्रित्य पुत्रैर्मे कृतं वैरं महारथैः ।\nतं सूततनयं तात कथं भीमो ह्ययोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relying on whom my sons, with their great chariot-warriors, made this enmity, how did Bhima fight that charioteer's son?"}},{"n":13,"text":"अनेकान्विप्रकारांश्च सूतपुत्रसमुद्भवान् ।\nस्मरमाणः कथं भीमो युयुधे सूतसूनुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering the many wrongs that came from the charioteer's son, how did Bhima fight the son of the charioteer?"}},{"n":14,"text":"योऽजयत्पृथिवीं सर्वां रथेनैकेन वीर्यवान् ।\nतं सूततनयं युद्धे कथं भीमो ह्ययोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one who conquered the whole earth with a single chariot, how did Bhima fight that son of a charioteer in battle?"}},{"n":15,"text":"यो जातः कुण्डलाभ्यां च कवचेन सहैव च ।\nतं सूतपुत्रं समरे भीमः कथमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who was born with earrings and armor, how did Bhima fight that charioteer's son in the battle?"}},{"n":16,"text":"यथा तयोर्युद्धमभूद्यश्चासीद्विजयी तयोः ।\nतन्ममाचक्ष्व तत्त्वेन कुशलो ह्यसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"How the fight between them went and which of them won, tell me truly, Sanjaya, for you are skilled."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु राधेयमुत्सृज्य रथिनां वरम् ।\nइयेष गन्तुं यत्रास्तां वीरौ कृष्णधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, leaving Radheya, best of chariot-fighters, wished to go where the two heroes Krishna and Dhananjaya were."}},{"n":18,"text":"तं प्रयान्तमभिद्रुत्य राधेयः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ।\nअभ्यवर्षन्महाराज मेघो वृष्ट्येव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he went, Radheya rushed after him and showered him with heron-feathered arrows, great king, as a cloud rains on a mountain."}},{"n":19,"text":"फुल्लता पङ्कजेनेव वक्त्रेणाभ्युत्स्मयन्बली ।\nआजुहाव रणे यान्तं भीममाधिरथिस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong son of Adhiratha, smiling with a face like a blooming lotus, challenged Bhima, who was passing, to battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"भीमसेनस्तदाह्वानं कर्णान्नामर्षयद्युधि ।\nअर्धमण्डलमावृत्य सूतपुत्रमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena could not bear Karna's challenge in the fight. He wheeled in a half circle and fought the charioteer's son."}},{"n":21,"text":"अवक्रगामिभिर्बाणैरभ्यवर्षन्महायसैः ।\nद्वैरथे दंशितं यत्तं सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He showered him with straight-flying great iron arrows, in single combat, the armored, steady best of all weapon-bearers."}},{"n":22,"text":"विधित्सुः कलहस्यान्तं जिघांसुः कर्णमक्षिणोत् ।\nतं च हत्वेतरान्सर्वान्हन्तुकामो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to end the quarrel and to kill Karna, the strong one set upon him, intending after killing him to kill all the others."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्मै प्रासृजदुग्राणि विविधानि परंतपः ।\nअमर्षी पाण्डवः क्रुद्धः शरवर्षाणि मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava, tormentor of foes, impatient and angry, sent at him fierce showers of arrows of many kinds, sir."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्य तानीषुवर्षाणि मत्तद्विरदगामिनः ।\nसूतपुत्रोऽस्त्रमायाभिरग्रसत्सुमहायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glorious son of the charioteer swallowed those showers of arrows of that rutting-elephant walker with the tricks of his weapon."}},{"n":25,"text":"स यथावन्महाराज विद्यया वै सुपूजितः ।\nआचार्यवन्महेष्वासः कर्णः पर्यचरद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, that great bowman Karna, well honored in the science, served in the battle like a teacher."}},{"n":26,"text":"संरम्भेण तु युध्यन्तं भीमसेनं स्मयन्निव ।\nअभ्यपद्यत राधेयस्तममर्षी वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya, impatient, came to Vrikodara, who fought with fury, smiling as it were."}},{"n":27,"text":"तन्नामृष्यत कौन्तेयः कर्णस्य स्मितमाहवे ।\nयुध्यमानेषु वीरेषु पश्यत्सु च समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti could not bear Karna's smile in the battle, while the heroes fought and all watched from around."}},{"n":28,"text":"तं भीमसेनः संप्राप्तं वत्सदन्तैः स्तनान्तरे ।\nविव्याध बलवान्क्रुद्धस्तोत्त्रैरिव महाद्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Karna came, strong Bhimasena in anger struck him between the breasts with calf-tooth arrows, as one prods a great elephant with goads."}},{"n":29,"text":"सूतं तु सूतपुत्रस्य सुपुङ्खैर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nसुमुक्तैश्चित्रवर्माणं निर्बिभेद त्रिसप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With well-feathered, sharp, well-loosed arrows he pierced the charioteer's son's charioteer, and Karna in his bright armor, three times seven."}},{"n":30,"text":"कर्णो जाम्बूनदैर्जालैः संछन्नान्वातरंहसः ।\nविव्याध तुरगान्वीरः पञ्चभिः पञ्चभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, the hero, with five arrows each struck the wind-swift horses, covered with nets of Jambunada gold."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो बाणमयं जालं भीमसेनरथं प्रति ।\nकर्णेन विहितं राजन्निमेषार्धाददृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the net of arrows that Karna spread toward Bhimasena's chariot, O king, was seen for half a blink."}},{"n":32,"text":"सरथः सध्वजस्तत्र ससूतः पाण्डवस्तदा ।\nप्राच्छाद्यत महाराज कर्णचापच्युतैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava, with chariot, banner and charioteer, was then covered, great king, by arrows shot from Karna's bow."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्य कर्णश्चतुःषष्ट्या व्यधमत्कवचं दृढम् ।\nक्रुद्धश्चाप्यहनत्पार्श्वे नाराचैर्मर्मभेदिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna broke his firm armor with sixty-four arrows, and angrily struck his sides with nitaracha arrows that pierce vital parts."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततोऽचिन्त्य महावेगान्कर्णकार्मुकनिःसृतान् ।\nसमाश्लिष्यदसंभ्रान्तः सूतपुत्रं वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vrikodara, unshaken, took in the arrows of fearsome speed loosed from Karna's bow and embraced the charioteer's son."}},{"n":35,"text":"स कर्णचापप्रभवानिषूनाशीविषोपमान् ।\nबिभ्रद्भीमो महाराज न जगाम व्यथां रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bearing those arrows from Karna's bow, like venomous snakes, Bhima, great king, felt no pain in the battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततो द्वात्रिंशता भल्लैर्निशितैस्तिग्मतेजनैः ।\nविव्याध समरे कर्णं भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the glorious Bhimasena pierced Karna in battle with thirty-two sharp, keen-pointed broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"अयत्नेनैव तं कर्णः शरैरुप समाकिरत् ।\nभीमसेनं महाबाहुं सैन्धवस्य वधैषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without effort Karna heaped arrows upon the mighty-armed Bhimasena, who was seeking Saindhava's death."}},{"n":38,"text":"मृदुपूर्वं च राधेयो भीममाजावयोधयत् ।\nक्रोधपूर्वं तथा भीमः पूर्ववैरमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya fought Bhima gently at first in the battle, and Bhima with anger at first, recalling the old enmity."}},{"n":39,"text":"तं भीमसेनो नामृष्यदवमानममर्षणः ।\nस तस्मै व्यसृजत्तूर्णं शरवर्षममित्रजित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, quick to anger, could not bear the slight; the conqueror of foes quickly sent a shower of arrows at him."}},{"n":40,"text":"ते शराः प्रेषिता राजन्भीमसेनेन संयुगे ।\nनिपेतुः सर्वतो भीमाः कूजन्त इव पक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows sent by Bhimasena in the battle fell everywhere, O king, terrible, like birds crying."}},{"n":41,"text":"हेमपुङ्खा महाराज भीमसेनधनुश्च्युताः ।\nअभ्यद्रवंस्ते राधेयं वृकाः क्षुद्रमृगं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gold-feathered, great king, shot from Bhimasena's bow, they rushed at Radheya like wolves at a small deer."}},{"n":42,"text":"कर्णस्तु रथिनां श्रेष्ठश्छाद्यमानः समन्ततः ।\nराजन्व्यसृजदुग्राणि शरवर्षाणि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, best of chariot-fighters, though covered on all sides, O king, loosed fierce showers of arrows in the battle."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्य तानशनिप्रख्यानिषून्समरशोभिनः ।\nचिच्छेद बहुभिर्भल्लैरसंप्राप्तान्वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrikodara cut those arrows, like thunderbolts and adorning the fight, with many broad-headed arrows before they reached him."}},{"n":44,"text":"पुनश्च शरवर्षेण छादयामास भारत ।\nकर्णो वैकर्तनो युद्धे भीमसेनं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And again, Bharata, Karna Vaikartana covered the great chariot-warrior Bhimasena in the battle with a shower of arrows."}},{"n":45,"text":"तत्र भारत भीमं तु दृष्टवन्तः स्म सायकैः ।\nसमाचिततनुं संख्ये श्वाविधं शललैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, Bharata, we saw Bhima with his body covered in arrows in the fight, like a porcupine with quills."}},{"n":46,"text":"हेमपुङ्खाञ्शिलाधौतान्कर्णचापच्युताञ्शरान् ।\nदधार समरे वीरः स्वरश्मीनिव भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero bore in the battle the gold-feathered arrows, whetted on stone, shot from Karna's bow, as the sun bears its own rays."}},{"n":47,"text":"रुधिरोक्षितसर्वाङ्गो भीमसेनो व्यरोचत ।\nतपनीयनिभैः पुष्पैः पलाश इव कानने ॥","meaning":{"en":"With all his limbs sprinkled with blood, Bhimasena shone like a palasha tree in a forest in bloom with flowers like gold."}},{"n":48,"text":"तत्तु भीमो महाराज कर्णस्य चरितं रणे ।\nनामृष्यत महेष्वासः क्रोधादुद्वृत्य चक्षुषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the great archer Bhima, great king, could not bear that deed of Karna's in the battle; with anger he rolled his eyes."}},{"n":49,"text":"स कर्णं पञ्चविंशत्या नाराचानां समार्पयत् ।\nमहीधरमिव श्वेतं गूढपादैर्विषोल्बणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Karna with twenty-five nitaracha arrows, like a white mountain with venomous snakes with hidden feet."}},{"n":50,"text":"तं विव्याध पुनर्भीमः षड्भिरष्टाभिरेव च ।\nमर्मस्वमरविक्रान्तः सूतपुत्रं महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, of divine valor, struck the charioteer's son in the vital parts again with six and with eight in the great battle."}},{"n":51,"text":"ततः कर्णस्य संक्रुद्धो भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nचिच्छेद कार्मुकं तूर्णं सर्वोपकरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the powerful Bhimasena, angry, quickly cut Karna's bow and all his implements."}},{"n":52,"text":"जघान चतुरश्चाश्वान्सूतं च त्वरितः शरैः ।\nनाराचैरर्करश्म्याभैः कर्णं विव्याध चोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck his four horses and his charioteer swiftly with arrows, and pierced Karna's chest with nitarachas gleaming like the sun's rays."}},{"n":53,"text":"ते जग्मुर्धरणीं सर्वे कर्णं निर्भिद्य मारिष ।\nयथा हि जलदं भित्त्वा राजन्सूर्यस्य रश्मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those arrows, sir, having pierced Karna, entered the earth, as the sun's rays pierce a cloud, O king."}},{"n":54,"text":"स वैकल्यं महत्प्राप्य छिन्नधन्वा शरार्दितः ।\nतथा पुरुषमानी स प्रत्यपायाद्रथान्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached great distress, his bow cut and tormented by arrows, he, proud of his manhood, withdrew to another chariot."}}]}]}